   "description": "The front after the First Battle of the Marne, which changed little until the German withdrawal to the Hindenburg Line began on 16 March 1917. Its northern part formed during the race to the sea (September to November 1914). Battles at Ypres, Verdun and the Somme moved parts of it by a few kilometres. Near Ypres the source map shows only the later line, so this line runs further east of Ypres there than the front of 1915 and 1916.",
